# Local OpenCode artifacts that must never be synced.
#
# Patterns here match the TARGET path (relative to ~), NOT the source path,
# so they are written `.config/opencode/...` rather than `dot_config/...`.
#
# They are inert while the file is absent from the source tree; they bite
# only if someone re-adds one, stopping chezmoi from writing it back out.
# They are NOT what protects an existing target file: on chezmoi v2.73.0,
# removing a source entry leaves the target file in place with or without
# this file.
.config/opencode/package.json
.config/opencode/package-lock.json
.config/opencode/bun.lock
.config/opencode/node_modules
.config/opencode/node_modules/**
# TUI settings, edited from Ctrl+P > Open settings. Machine-local.
.config/opencode/cli.json
# Holds the background-service password. Secret, never tracked.
.config/opencode/service.json

# Ignore Hyprland configs - Caelestia will manage them
.config/hypr/

# Ignore fish configs - Caelestia will manage them
.config/fish/
